## Test Smell Audit — Academic Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10) | **Scope:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests` (7 test methods)  
**Integration calibration applied** — class is marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test (Smell #3)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` **Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← Hard 3-second wall-clock wait
```

**Why still High for integration tests:** Even in integration scope, a hard sleep is non-deterministic — the event may arrive in 50ms or require 5s under CI load. This makes the suite slow *and* flaky.

**Fix:**
```csharp
// Poll with timeout instead of sleeping
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(50, cts.Token);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell #1)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` **Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Risk:** One branch *never* executes — you're unknowingly testing only half the logic. If the wrong type is returned, the test still passes via the other branch.

**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests with deterministic setup:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell #4)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` **Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← No assertion — passes even if all inserts silently fail
}
```

**Risk:** False confidence — the test always passes as long as no exception is thrown. Data corruption or silent failures go undetected.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Catalog)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` **Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
// ← 4 assertions, zero descriptive messages
```

**Risk:** When one fails in CI, the error message is `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>` with no context about *which property* was wrong or why.

**Fix:** Add message parameters:
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Database should assign a positive ID");
```

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The following tests are well-structured:

| Method | Why it's good |
|--------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert, focused behavior |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single concern, null-check assertion is expressive |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count (3) is contextually obvious (not magic), uses `CollectionAssert` |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Legitimate integration concern, clean async pattern |

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Rationale |
|----------|-------|--------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~2 min | Prevents false-pass; one-line addition |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Eliminates hidden dead branch |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~5 min | Reduces flakiness + saves 3s per run |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | ~3 min | Improves CI debuggability |

**Overall verdict:** 4 of 7 tests are clean. The 3 high-severity findings are straightforward to fix and would meaningfully improve reliability and diagnostic speed.
